To incorporate the `ABOR` and `HELP` commands into the existing sequence of FTP client requests, we can place the `HELP` command after the `SYST` command to get information about available commands or help, and the `ABOR` command can be placed after the `LIST` command to abort any ongoing command if necessary. Here is the modified sequence of client requests:

```
USER anonymous
PASS ubuntu
SYST
HELP
PWD
PORT 127,0,0,1,152,193
LIST
ABOR
QUIT
```

This modified sequence retains the logical flow of the FTP commands while including the requested `ABOR` and `HELP` commands

